    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Maple Shade Train Station, built in the 19th century, remains a landmark of the township’s early rail history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mapleshadehistory.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1950, the Mary’s Cafe sit‑in in Maple Shade became one of the first non‑violent civil‑rights protests in the nation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maple_Shade_Township%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The township’s 2026 250th‑anniversary celebrations, led by the Historical Society, highlighted Maple Shade’s long‑standing heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://mapleshadehistory.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Maple Shade’s downtown Main Street was revitalized through historic preservation efforts that emphasize the town’s unique character.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
